course: dictionary
lesson: 12063
title: The sorter called classifier
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A classifier is a person or thing that sorts things into groups. When you put your toys into boxes for cars, dolls and books, you are doing a classifier's job. Scientists do this too, sorting animals into groups by what they look like.
explain: «The librarian is a classifier who puts each book on the right shelf.» The clue is the word sorts. A librarian decides which group each book belongs to, so classifier here means a person who sorts things.
explain: In computing, a classifier is a program that learns from examples. «The email classifier sent the strange message to the spam folder.» The program learned what spam looks like, then used that to label new emails.
explain: Words can be classifiers too. In Mandarin, «ge» is a common classifier. It sits between a number and a noun, just like «a piece of» in English, which helps show what kind of thing you are counting.
fact: A classifier is a person or thing that sorts things into groups.
fact: To classify means to sort things into groups, so a classifier is the one doing the sorting.
fact: In computing, a classifier learns from examples to label new things, like spam or not spam.
fact: In Mandarin, «ge» is a common classifier, used between a number and a noun.
fact: In English, «a piece of» works in a similar way, as in «a piece of cake».
exercise: «The classifier sorted the animals into birds, fish and insects.» What is a classifier here? | A map of the sea | A type of animal | A loud noise made by a bird | *A thing or person that sorts things into groups
exercise: A computer classifier learns from examples. What does it do? | It keeps the screen cool | *It labels new things, like spam or not spam | It plays music for the user | It draws pictures of animals
exercise: In Mandarin, «ge» is a classifier. Which English phrase is most like it? | a very big | quickly | in the morning | *a piece of
test: «The classifier put every email into spam or not spam.» What job does the classifier do? | Writes brand new emails | *Sorts emails into groups | Turns the computer off | Sends emails to the moon
test: Why might a scientist use a classifier key? | To make the animals run faster | *To sort animals into groups | To count the stones on a beach | To hide animals from people
exam: «A classifier learns from examples, then labels new things.» Which description fits best? | *A program that learns from examples and sorts new things into groups | A toy that makes a noise when you touch it | A word that means very old | A person who paints pictures of the sea
